%SIXMD 1
# @?LS - LIST DIRECTORY CONTENTS

## @?OPERANDS

### @?[PATH ...]
FILES OR DIRECTORIES TO LIST.  THE CURRENT DIRECTORY IS USED WHEN OMITTED.

## DESCRIPTION

LS PRINTS A FILE PATH DIRECTLY OR LISTS EACH ENTRY OF A DIRECTORY.  DIRECTORY
ENTRIES ARE PREFIXED WITH D FOR DIRECTORY, M FOR MOUNT SOURCE, B FOR BLOCK
DEVICE, C FOR CHARACTER DEVICE, OR F FOR OTHER FILE TYPES.
USAGE IS 'LS [PATH ...]'.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - SUCCESS
### @?1 - OPERATION FAILED OR CONDITION FALSE
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE WHEN APPLICABLE
